groupRows is operation
groupRows purpose "Group a source's tokens into words and the words into rows, one row per line that has words"
groupRows invariant rowsOfWords "Each line with words becomes one row of its words in order, each word located by line and column; a line with no words (blank, or only a comment) becomes no row"
groupRows invariant joinsDottedNames "Identifiers joined by dots with no space between them are one name word"
groupRows invariant negativeIntegers "A minus sign written directly before digits makes one negative integer word that starts at the sign"
groupRows invariant rejectsMalformedWords "A mark that is not a dot inside a name or a minus before digits is strayMark, two tokens with no space between them are gluedWords, and a name ending in a dot is danglingDot"
groupRows invariant rejectsShortRows "A row of fewer than three words is shortRow at its first word"
groupRows typeParameter none
groupRows input source String borrowed
groupRows input tokens lexer.Tokens borrowed
groupRows input words Words borrowedMutable
groupRows input rows Rows borrowedMutable
groupRows output none
groupRows outputOwnedBy none
groupRows raises Rejection
groupRows effect none
groupRows uses none
groupRows memoryHeap false
groupRows async false
groupRows maxRecursion none
groupRows label begin loopKind none
groupRows label begin within none
groupRows label visit note "Every token is visited once; the list's length, read first, bounds the loop"
groupRows label visit loopKind forEach
groupRows label visit within none
groupRows label visit maxIterations tokenCount
